## What I do

I'm a Senior Frontend Engineer who cares deeply about how systems feel. Most of my work sits one
level below the product: the components, the patterns, and the guardrails other engineers build
on top of.

The problems that keep my attention are the recurring ones — inconsistent UI patterns across
teams, components that break in ways nobody predicted, and design systems that look complete in
Figma and fall apart on the way to production. Moving a team from scattered implementations to
structured patterns is slow work, but it is the work that reduces regressions and makes everything
after it faster.

## How I think about it

Accessibility is a production concern, not an audit item. Component APIs are a form of
documentation. Architecture is mostly about which decisions you can afford to get wrong.

